>In article <94053.143211K2002E1@ALIJKU11.BITNET>,
>Warrior Of Darkness  <K2002E1@ALIJKU11.BITNET> wrote:
>>*argl* I was playing as a Valkyrie, dungeon level 6, Exp. level 11, 17000 Exp.
>>Max.HP 95 when I noticed my Max HP suddenly decreasing. In the end I only had
>>65 Max HP left. Is this normal or can I do anything against it?
>
>It's not normal, it's been reported before, and nobody has _any_ idea what
>causes it...  (what version was this?)

Any chance that you were polymorphing when this was happening?  Any time 
a polymorph fails, you have a chance of your stats (including your max 
hit points) changing.  This happens with amulets of change, or a failed
polymorph from a trap, a wand, or a ring.

The most likely way for this to happen without you noticing is wandering
around, hitting a polymorph trap.  Not noticing the message "You feel a 
change coming over you.  You feel like a new man!", and getting your
max hitpoints re-rolled.  It'd be pretty easy to miss this message in the
middle of a fight.

Other things which could lower your max hp:
   - Poison attack it you're not resistant
   - Sometimes if you die and your life is saved, you wind up with a 
     new max hp (only happens in strange situations)
   - Level draining attacks (eg: Stormbringer, Vampire Lords, ...)

That's about all I can think of.  If none of that was happening (ie: no
level drains, you have magic resistance (to protect against polymorph 
traps) and poison resistance, you weren't wearing a ring of polymorph,
and you haven't died, then maybe it is a bug.
